  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Results for $[5,2,0]^2$ (2026-10-02, P1 $=(h,\\theta)=(1/2,\\{2/7,-3/5\\})$, 300 digits; Sections 1–6b about 8 min, 6c about 1 min)\n- **Checks.** The quantum determinant, commutativity and $\\Omega$ eigen-covector checks pass to $\\le10^{-287}$. The chain identity holds to $10^{-237}$. There are 28 HW states in 18 sectors: multiplicity 2 at $[9,4,1]$, $[9,3,2]$, $[8,5,1]$, $[7,6,1]$, $[7,4,3]$, $[6,5,3]$, and **multiplicity 3** at $[8,4,2]$ and $[7,5,2]$.\n- **Site-1 localization (new; Section 4).** For $\\lambda_1\\le5$ and $c=-7..1$, the nontrivial site-1-local shapes are exactly **$T_{(1,1)},T_{(2,2)},T_{(3,3)},T_{(4,3)},T_{(5,3)}$ at $\\theta_1-5h$**.\n  - **Unified rule** (fits all nine reps $[2,1,0]\\dots[5,4,0]$): with $d=\\lambda_1-\\lambda_2$, the insertions are $T_{(k,k)}$ for $k=1..d$ and $T_{(k,d)}$ for $k=d+1..\\lambda_1$, all at $\\theta_1-\\lambda_1h$. That is $\\lambda_1$ insertions in total.\n- **Prefactors** (fitted at P1; each ansatz match is unique; checked at P2 to $10^{-289}$), with $t=\\theta_{12}/h$:\n  - $f_{(1,1)}=(t-3)(t-6)$;\n  - $f_{(2,2)}=(t-2)(t-3)(t-5)(t-6)$;\n  - $f_{(3,3)}=(t-1)(t-2)(t-3)(t-4)(t-5)(t-6)$;\n  - $f_{(4,3)}=(t-1)(t-2)^2(t-3)(t-4)(t-5)(t-6)$;\n  - $f_{(5,3)}=(t-1)^2(t-2)^2(t-3)(t-4)(t-5)(t-6)$.\n- **Structural.** The contamination ratios of all 27 non-top HW states are $\\varphi,\\omega$-independent, with spread $\\le10^{-3.9}$ at $\\varepsilon=10^{-5}$.\n- **End to end, site 1 + $\\langle\\Omega|\\Psi\\rangle$ only.** All 27 non-top HW states are recovered from Q-side numbers, scale included.\n  - **Section 6** (fit at $10^{-5}$): errors are $10^{-3.0}$–$10^{-5.7}$ at $(10^{-4},\\varphi)$ and $10^{-3.3}$–$10^{-7.1}$ at $(10^{-5},\\varphi')$, with $\\ge199$ digits.\n  - **Section 6b** (refit at $10^{-6}$): errors are $10^{-4.3}$–$10^{-8.1}$ at $(10^{-6},\\varphi')$, with $\\ge183$ digits.\n  - **Section 6c (weak sectors).** The two worst errors come from weakly conditioned sector spaces: $[7,6,1]$ copy 2 ($\\sigma_2=0.025$) and $[7,4,3]$ copy 2 ($\\sigma_2=0.019$). They still scale like $O(\\varepsilon)$, but are amplified by $\\sim1/\\sigma_2$. Per-copy cleaning lowers them to $10^{-6.2}$ and $10^{-5.7}$. With that choice, **every state is at $\\le10^{-5.5}$ at $\\varepsilon=10^{-6}$**.\n  - **Per-copy cleaning is required** (sector HW rank deficient) for $[9,3,2]$, $[8,5,1]$, $[8,4,2]$ (multiplicity 3; sector rank 2) and $[7,5,2]$ (multiplicity 3; sector rank 2). It is advisable for $[7,6,1]$ and $[7,4,3]$.\n  - Sector-wide works well for $[9,4,1]$ ($\\sigma_2=0.010$, but errors $\\le10^{-6.9}$ at $10^{-6}$), $[6,5,3]$ (0.33), all multiplicity-1 sectors, and the bottom irrep $[5,5,4]$.\n- **Caveats.** The clean coefficients are fitted numerically, not in closed form. There is one chain point for the pipeline. The eigenvalues are read from the eigenvectors and stand in for the Q's.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  }
 ],
